IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc25-remediation-negotiation.l4 -- Part XXII.1 Remediation Agreements of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: sections 715.3 to 715.35
-- (definitions, acting on a victim's behalf, purpose, the conditions for negotiating, the notice, the contents of the agreement, the independent monitor).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. It takes nobody's point of view. The seat layer (ccc25-seat.l4) asks the accused's questions and calls these rules.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. The French equivalents in parentheses after a defined term are quoted, not encoded.
--
-- HOW A RESULT READS (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc25)"):
--   JUST TRUE   the facts bring the case within the rule, on the text's own words.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, a flat negative, a condition introduced by "if", "where", "when", "while", "except", "unless").
--   NOTHING     not covered: the text lists without closing the list, says "includes", is silent, points outside the sources, or limits a grant or
--               prohibition in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- A function NAMED for a grant or a power ("may") answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE, when an "if" gate fails (the coordinator's ruling of 2026-11-12); each such site has one fork line in NOTES.md.
--
-- SEAMS (PLAN.md section 6, row ccc25): the answers of other parts are INPUTS named for the section they come from, typed MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   `s 2 organization`, `s 2 victim`, `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` (keel), `s 2.2 ...` (keel), `Schedule to Part XXII.1 the offence is listed` (ccc29).

§ `Section 715.3 -- Definitions (Part XXII.1)`

-- 715.3 (1) lead-in "The following definitions apply in this Part." has no rule of its own: it sets the scope of the five definitions below (coverage row, inert, reason 1).

-- court means a superior court of criminal jurisdiction but does not include a court of appeal.
-- src:14875 | court means a superior court of criminal jurisdiction but does not include a court of appeal. (tribunal)
@ref s 715.3(1) "court" (src:14875-14875)
GIVEN `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the body is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body is a court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.3(1) court` MEANS
    IF `the body is a court of appeal`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include a court of appeal"
    ELSE `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the body is one`   -- JUST TRUE, or the text's own "means" no (s 2), or NOTHING when s 2 is not covered

-- offence means any offence listed in the schedule to this Part. The schedule is in another part's range: its answer is an input.
-- src:14876 | offence means any offence listed in the schedule to this Part. (infraction)
@ref s 715.3(1) "offence" (src:14876-14876)
GIVEN `Schedule to Part XXII.1 the offence is listed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.3(1) offence` MEANS `Schedule to Part XXII.1 the offence is listed`   -- JUST FALSE is the text's own "means any offence listed in the schedule"; NOTHING only if the schedule's answer is not covered

-- organization has the same meaning as in section 2 but does not include a public body, trade union or municipality.
-- src:14877 | organization has the same meaning as in section 2 but does not include a public body, trade union or municipality. (organisation)
@ref s 715.3(1) "organization" (src:14877-14877)
GIVEN `s 2 organization: the body is an organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body is a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a trade union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a municipality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.3(1) organization` MEANS
    IF `the body is a public body` OR `the body is a trade union` OR `the body is a municipality`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include a public body, trade union or municipality"
    ELSE `s 2 organization: the body is an organization`   -- "has the same meaning as in section 2": JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING exactly as s 2 answers

-- remediation agreement means an agreement, between an organization accused of having committed an offence and a prosecutor, to stay any proceedings related to that offence
-- if the organization complies with the terms of the agreement. "Organization" and "offence" are this Part's own terms (the answers of the two functions above).
-- src:14878 | remediation agreement means an agreement, between an organization accused of having committed an offence and a prosecutor, to stay any proceedings related to that offence if the organization complies with the terms of the agreement. (accord de réparation)
@ref s 715.3(1) "remediation agreement" (src:14878-14878)
GIVEN `it is an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one party is an organization, by s 715.3(1) organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the organization is accused of having committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an offence, by s 715.3(1) offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the other party is a prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is to stay any proceedings related to that offence if the organization complies with the terms of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is an agreement` AND `the organization is accused of having committed the offence` AND `the other party is a prosecutor` AND `the agreement is to stay any proceedings related to that offence if the organization complies with the terms of the agreement`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "remediation agreement means an agreement, between an organization accused of having committed an offence and a prosecutor, to stay any proceedings related to that offence"
        IF (`one party is an organization, by s 715.3(1) organization` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the offence is an offence, by s 715.3(1) offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "between an organization accused of having committed an offence and a prosecutor"
        IF (`one party is an organization, by s 715.3(1) organization` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the offence is an offence, by s 715.3(1) offence` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the organization and offence answers come from s 2 and the Schedule, and one of them is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- victim has the same meaning as in section 2 but, with respect to an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, it includes any person outside Canada.
-- src:14879 | victim has the same meaning as in section 2 but, with respect to an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, it includes any person outside Canada. (victime)
@ref s 715.3(1) "victim" (src:14879-14879)
GIVEN `s 2 victim: the person is a victim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.3(1) victim` MEANS
    IF `the offence is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` AND `the person is a person outside Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `s 2 victim: the person is a victim`   -- "has the same meaning as in section 2": JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING exactly as s 2 answers

-- 715.3 (2) For the purposes of this Part, a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may also act on a victim's behalf when authorized to do so by the court, if the victim requests it or the prosecutor deems it appropriate.
-- "Not referred to in section 2.2" is read as: s 2.2 does not answer JUST TRUE for the third party (fork F1). "When authorized ... by the court" is a "when" gate (listed, answer JUST FALSE);
-- "if the victim requests it or the prosecutor deems it appropriate" is an "if" gate on a grant (flipped to NOTHING, fork F2).
-- src:14881 | (2) For the purposes of this Part, a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may also act on a victim’s behalf when authorized to do so by the court, if the victim requests it or the prosecutor deems it appropriate.
@ref s 715.3(2) (src:14881-14881)
GIVEN `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court has authorized the third party to act on the victim’s behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim requests that the third party act on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor deems it appropriate that the third party act on the victim’s behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.3(2) a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may act on the victim’s behalf` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a third party not referred to in section 2.2"
        IF NOT `the court has authorized the third party to act on the victim’s behalf` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when authorized to do so by the court"
        IF `the victim requests that the third party act on their behalf` OR `the prosecutor deems it appropriate that the third party act on the victim’s behalf` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the victim requests it or the prosecutor deems it appropriate"

§ `Section 715.31 -- Purpose (Part XXII.1)`

-- 715.31 The purpose of this Part is to establish a remediation agreement regime ... that has the following objectives: (a) to denounce ...; (b) to hold the organization accountable ...; (c) to contribute to respect for the law ...;
-- (d) to encourage voluntary disclosure ...; (e) to provide reparations ...; (f) to reduce the negative consequences ... The clause states a purpose and creates no rule: coverage rows, inert, reason 1.
-- The text is kept here as quotation only, so that a reader holding the source beside this module sees nothing skipped.
-- src:14883 | 715.31 The purpose of this Part is to establish a remediation agreement regime that is applicable to organizations alleged to have committed an offence and that has the following objectives:
-- src:14884 | (a) to denounce an organization’s wrongdoing and the harm that the wrongdoing has caused to victims or to the community;
-- src:14885 | (b) to hold the organization accountable for its wrongdoing through effective, proportionate and dissuasive penalties;
-- src:14886 | (c) to contribute to respect for the law by imposing an obligation on the organization to put in place corrective measures and promote a compliance culture;
-- src:14887 | (d) to encourage voluntary disclosure of the wrongdoing;
-- src:14888 | (e) to provide reparations for harm done to victims or to the community; and
-- src:14889 | (f) to reduce the negative consequences of the wrongdoing for persons — employees, customers, pensioners and others — who did not engage in the wrongdoing, while holding responsible those individuals who did engage in that wrongdoing.
@ref s 715.31 (src:14883-14889)
`s 715.31 the purpose of this Part as the text states it` MEANS "to establish a remediation agreement regime that is applicable to organizations alleged to have committed an offence"

§ `Section 715.32 -- Conditions for remediation agreement`

-- 715.32 (1) The prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement with an organization alleged to have committed an offence if the following conditions are met: (a) ... (d).
-- A grant ("may") with an "if" gate: when a condition is not met the answer is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (fork F2). The text does not say "only if". Opinions are the prosecutor's: they are inputs, never guessed.
-- src:14891 | 715.32 (1) The prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement with an organization alleged to have committed an offence if the following conditions are met:
-- src:14892 | (a) the prosecutor is of the opinion that there is a reasonable prospect of conviction with respect to the offence;
-- src:14893 | (b) the prosecutor is of the opinion that the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence did not cause and was not likely to have caused serious bodily harm or death, or injury to national defence or national security, and was not committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization or terrorist group;
-- src:14894 | (c) the prosecutor is of the opinion that negotiating the agreement is in the public interest and appropriate in the circumstances; and
-- src:14895 | (d) the Attorney General has consented to the negotiation of the agreement.
@ref s 715.32(1) (src:14891-14895)
GIVEN `the body is an organization, by s 715.3(1) organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the organization is alleged to have committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an offence, by s 715.3(1) offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor is of the opinion that there is a reasonable prospect of conviction with respect to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence did not cause and was not likely to have caused serious bodily harm or death, or injury to national defence or national security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the act or omission was not committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization or terrorist group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor is of the opinion that negotiating the agreement is in the public interest and appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General has consented to the negotiation of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the body is an organization, by s 715.3(1) organization` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the offence is an offence, by s 715.3(1) offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the organization is alleged to have committed the offence`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with an organization alleged to have committed an offence"
        IF (`the body is an organization, by s 715.3(1) organization` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the offence is an offence, by s 715.3(1) offence` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the organization and offence answers come from s 2 and the Schedule
        IF NOT (`the prosecutor is of the opinion that there is a reasonable prospect of conviction with respect to the offence` AND `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence did not cause and was not likely to have caused serious bodily harm or death, or injury to national defence or national security` AND `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the act or omission was not committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization or terrorist group` AND `the prosecutor is of the opinion that negotiating the agreement is in the public interest and appropriate in the circumstances` AND `the Attorney General has consented to the negotiation of the agreement`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the following conditions are met"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 715.32 (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), the prosecutor must consider the following factors: (a) to (i). A duty on the prosecutor. Paragraph (i), "any other factor that the prosecutor considers relevant",
-- brings in a factor only if the prosecutor considers it relevant; the list is not closed with "only", so another factor the prosecutor does not consider relevant is NOT COVERED.
-- src:14897 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), the prosecutor must consider the following factors:
-- src:14898 | (a) the circumstances in which the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence was brought to the attention of investigative authorities;
-- src:14899 | (b) the nature and gravity of the act or omission and its impact on any victim;
-- src:14900 | (c) the degree of involvement of senior officers of the organization in the act or omission;
-- src:14901 | (d) whether the organization has taken disciplinary action, including termination of employment, against any person who was involved in the act or omission;
-- src:14902 | (e) whether the organization has made reparations or taken other measures to remedy the harm caused by the act or omission and to prevent the commission of similar acts or omissions;
-- src:14903 | (f) whether the organization has identified or expressed a willingness to identify any person involved in wrongdoing related to the act or omission;
-- src:14904 | (g) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — was convicted of an offence or sanctioned by a regulatory body, or whether it entered into a previous remediation agreement or other settlement, in Canada or elsewhere, for similar acts or omissions;
-- src:14905 | (h) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — is alleged to have committed any other offences, including those not listed in the schedule to this Part; and
-- src:14906 | (i) any other factor that the prosecutor considers relevant.
@ref s 715.32(2) (src:14897-14906)
DECLARE `s 715.32(2) the factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.32(2)(a) the circumstances in which the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence was brought to the attention of investigative authorities`
    `s 715.32(2)(b) the nature and gravity of the act or omission and its impact on any victim`
    `s 715.32(2)(c) the degree of involvement of senior officers of the organization in the act or omission`
    `s 715.32(2)(d) whether the organization has taken disciplinary action, including termination of employment, against any person who was involved in the act or omission`
    `s 715.32(2)(e) whether the organization has made reparations or taken other measures to remedy the harm caused by the act or omission and to prevent the commission of similar acts or omissions`
    `s 715.32(2)(f) whether the organization has identified or expressed a willingness to identify any person involved in wrongdoing related to the act or omission`
    `s 715.32(2)(g) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — was convicted of an offence or sanctioned by a regulatory body, or whether it entered into a previous remediation agreement or other settlement, in Canada or elsewhere, for similar acts or omissions`
    `s 715.32(2)(h) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — is alleged to have committed any other offences, including those not listed in the schedule to this Part`
    `s 715.32(2)(i) any other factor that the prosecutor considers relevant`

@ref s 715.32(2) (src:14897-14906)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 715.32(2) the factor`
      `the prosecutor considers the factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 715.32(2)(a) the circumstances in which the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence was brought to the attention of investigative authorities` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.32(2)(b) the nature and gravity of the act or omission and its impact on any victim` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.32(2)(c) the degree of involvement of senior officers of the organization in the act or omission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.32(2)(d) whether the organization has taken disciplinary action, including termination of employment, against any person who was involved in the act or omission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.32(2)(e) whether the organization has made reparations or taken other measures to remedy the harm caused by the act or omission and to prevent the commission of similar acts or omissions` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.32(2)(f) whether the organization has identified or expressed a willingness to identify any person involved in wrongdoing related to the act or omission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.32(2)(g) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — was convicted of an offence or sanctioned by a regulatory body, or whether it entered into a previous remediation agreement or other settlement, in Canada or elsewhere, for similar acts or omissions` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.32(2)(h) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — is alleged to have committed any other offences, including those not listed in the schedule to this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.32(2)(i) any other factor that the prosecutor considers relevant` THEN IF `the prosecutor considers the factor relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any other factor that the prosecutor considers relevant"

-- 715.32 (3) Despite paragraph (2)(i), if the organization is alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, the prosecutor must not consider
-- the national economic interest, the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada or the identity of the organization or individual involved. A bar on the prosecutor, with an "if".
-- src:14908 | (3) Despite paragraph (2)(i), if the organization is alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, the prosecutor must not consider the national economic interest, the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada or the identity of the organization or individual involved.
@ref s 715.32(3) (src:14908-14908)
DECLARE `s 715.32(3) the matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.32(3) the national economic interest`
    `s 715.32(3) the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada`
    `s 715.32(3) the identity of the organization or individual involved`
    `s 715.32(3) a matter that none of those names`

@ref s 715.32(3) (src:14908-14908)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 715.32(3) the matter`
      `the organization is alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.32(3) the prosecutor must not consider the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT `the organization is alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the organization is alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act"
    ELSE CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `s 715.32(3) the national economic interest` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.32(3) the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.32(3) the identity of the organization or individual involved` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.32(3) a matter that none of those names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the national economic interest, the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada or the identity of the organization or individual involved"

§ `Section 715.33 -- Notice to organization: invitation to negotiate`

-- 715.33 (1) If the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement, they must give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations and the notice must include (a) to (j).
-- Two functions: whether the duty to give the notice arises (the "if"), and whether a notice meets the content requirement.
-- src:14910 | 715.33 (1) If the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement, they must give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations and the notice must include
@ref s 715.33(1) (src:14910-14910)
GIVEN `the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.33(1) the prosecutor must give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement"

-- src:14910 | 715.33 (1) If the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement, they must give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations and the notice must include
-- src:14911 | (a) a summary description of the offence to which the agreement would apply;
-- src:14912 | (b) an indication of the voluntary nature of the negotiation process;
-- src:14913 | (c) an indication of the legal effects of the agreement;
-- src:14914 | (d) an indication that, by agreeing to the terms of this notice, the organization explicitly waives the inclusion of the negotiation period and the period during which the agreement is in force in any assessment of the reasonableness of the delay between the day on which the charge is laid and the end of trial;
-- src:14915 | (e) an indication that negotiations must be carried out in good faith and that the organization must provide all information requested by the prosecutor that the organization is aware of or can obtain through reasonable efforts, including information enabling the identification of any person involved in the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence or any wrongdoing related to that act or omission;
-- src:14916 | (f) an indication of how the information disclosed by the organization during the negotiations may be used, subject to subsection (2);
-- src:14917 | (g) a warning that knowingly making false or misleading statements or knowingly providing false or misleading information during the negotiations may lead to the recommencement of proceedings or prosecution for obstruction of justice;
-- src:14918 | (h) an indication that either party may withdraw from the negotiations by providing written notice to the other party;
-- src:14919 | (i) an indication that reasonable efforts must be made by both parties to identify any victim as soon as practicable; and
-- src:14920 | (j) a deadline to accept the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice.
@ref s 715.33(1) (src:14910-14920)
DECLARE `s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` HAS
    `the notice is written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations given to the organization`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(a) a summary description of the offence to which the agreement would apply`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b) an indication of the voluntary nature of the negotiation process`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c) an indication of the legal effects of the agreement`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(d) an indication that, by agreeing to the terms of this notice, the organization explicitly waives the inclusion of the negotiation period and the period during which the agreement is in force in any assessment of the reasonableness of the delay between the day on which the charge is laid and the end of trial`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(e) an indication that negotiations must be carried out in good faith and that the organization must provide all information requested by the prosecutor that the organization is aware of or can obtain through reasonable efforts, including information enabling the identification of any person involved in the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence or any wrongdoing related to that act or omission`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(f) an indication of how the information disclosed by the organization during the negotiations may be used, subject to subsection (2)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(g) a warning that knowingly making false or misleading statements or knowingly providing false or misleading information during the negotiations may lead to the recommencement of proceedings or prosecution for obstruction of justice`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(h) an indication that either party may withdraw from the negotiations by providing written notice to the other party`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i) an indication that reasonable efforts must be made by both parties to identify any victim as soon as practicable`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(j) a deadline to accept the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 715.33(1) (src:14910-14920)
GIVEN notice IS A `s 715.33(1) what the notice includes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` MEANS
    IF     notice's `the notice is written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations given to the organization`
       AND notice's `(a) a summary description of the offence to which the agreement would apply`
       AND notice's `(b) an indication of the voluntary nature of the negotiation process`
       AND notice's `(c) an indication of the legal effects of the agreement`
       AND notice's `(d) an indication that, by agreeing to the terms of this notice, the organization explicitly waives the inclusion of the negotiation period and the period during which the agreement is in force in any assessment of the reasonableness of the delay between the day on which the charge is laid and the end of trial`
       AND notice's `(e) an indication that negotiations must be carried out in good faith and that the organization must provide all information requested by the prosecutor that the organization is aware of or can obtain through reasonable efforts, including information enabling the identification of any person involved in the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence or any wrongdoing related to that act or omission`
       AND notice's `(f) an indication of how the information disclosed by the organization during the negotiations may be used, subject to subsection (2)`
       AND notice's `(g) a warning that knowingly making false or misleading statements or knowingly providing false or misleading information during the negotiations may lead to the recommencement of proceedings or prosecution for obstruction of justice`
       AND notice's `(h) an indication that either party may withdraw from the negotiations by providing written notice to the other party`
       AND notice's `(i) an indication that reasonable efforts must be made by both parties to identify any victim as soon as practicable`
       AND notice's `(j) a deadline to accept the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they must give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations and the notice must include"

-- 715.33 (2) No admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission made by the organization during the negotiations is admissible in evidence against that organization
-- in any civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission, except those contained in the statement of facts or admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs 715.34(1)(a) and (b),
-- if the parties reach an agreement and it is approved by the court. A flat negative with an exception: once the exception is met the subsection no longer says the statement is inadmissible (JUST FALSE, fork F3).
-- src:14922 | (2) No admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission made by the organization during the negotiations is admissible in evidence against that organization in any civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission, except those contained in the statement of facts or admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs 715.34(1)(a) and (b), if the parties reach an agreement and it is approved by the court.
@ref s 715.33(2) (src:14922-14922)
GIVEN `it is an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made by the organization during the negotiations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is offered in evidence against that organization in civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is contained in the statement of facts or admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs 715.34(1)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties reach an agreement and it is approved by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.33(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission` AND `it was made by the organization during the negotiations` AND `it is offered in evidence against that organization in civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "made by the organization during the negotiations is admissible in evidence against that organization in any civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission"
        IF `it is contained in the statement of facts or admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs 715.34(1)(a) and (b)` AND `the parties reach an agreement and it is approved by the court` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except those contained in the statement of facts or admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs 715.34(1)(a) and (b), if the parties reach an agreement and it is approved by the court"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 715.34 -- Contents of the agreement`

-- 715.34 (1) A remediation agreement must include (a) to (p). The agreement is a thing, not a party: the requirement is a test over what the agreement includes (no duty-bearer is named).
-- Where a requirement is not met the function answers JUST FALSE (the text states the requirement with "must include": the bare "must" site, fork F4).
-- src:14924 | 715.34 (1) A remediation agreement must include
-- src:14925 | (a) a statement of facts related to the offence that the organization is alleged to have committed and an undertaking by the organization not to make or condone any public statement that contradicts those facts;
-- src:14926 | (b) the organization’s admission of responsibility for the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence;
-- src:14927 | (c) an indication of the obligation for the organization to provide any other information that will assist in identifying any person involved in the act or omission, or any wrongdoing related to that act or omission, that the organization becomes aware of, or can obtain through reasonable efforts, after the agreement has been entered into;
-- src:14928 | (d) an indication of the obligation for the organization to cooperate in any investigation, prosecution or other proceeding in Canada — or elsewhere if the prosecutor considers it appropriate — resulting from the act or omission, including by providing information or testimony;
-- src:14929 | (e) with respect to any property, benefit or advantage identified in the agreement that was obtained or derived directly or indirectly from the act or omission, an obligation for the organization to
-- src:14930 | (i) forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of Canada, to be disposed of in accordance with paragraph 4(1)(b.2) of the Seized Property Management Act,
-- src:14931 | (ii) forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of a province, to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs, or
-- src:14932 | (iii) otherwise deal with it, as the prosecutor directs;
-- src:14933 | (f) an indication of the obligation for the organization to pay a penalty to the Receiver General or to the treasurer of a province, as the case may be, for each offence to which the agreement applies, the amount to be paid and any other terms respecting payment;
-- src:14934 | (g) an indication of any reparations, including restitution consistent with paragraph 738(1)(a) or (b), that the organization is required to make to a victim or a statement by the prosecutor of the reasons why reparations to a victim are not appropriate in the circumstances and an indication of any measure required in lieu of reparations to a victim;
-- src:14935 | (h) an indication of the obligation for the organization to pay a victim surcharge for each offence to which the agreement applies, other than an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, the amount to be paid and any other terms respecting payment;
-- src:14936 | (i) an indication of the obligation for the organization to report to the prosecutor on the implementation of the agreement and an indication of the manner in which the report is to be made and any other terms respecting reporting;
-- src:14937 | (j) an indication of the legal effects of the agreement;
-- src:14938 | (k) an acknowledgement by the organization that the agreement has been made in good faith and that the information it has provided during the negotiation is accurate and complete and a commitment that it will continue to provide accurate and complete information while the agreement is in force;
-- src:14939 | (l) an indication of the use that can be made of information obtained as a result of the agreement, subject to subsection (2);
-- src:14940 | (m) a warning that the breach of any term of the agreement may lead to an application by the prosecutor for termination of the agreement and a recommencement of proceedings;
-- src:14941 | (n) an indication of the obligation for the organization not to deduct, for income tax purposes, the costs of any reparations or other measures referred to in paragraph (g) or any other costs incurred to fulfil the terms of the agreement;
-- src:14942 | (o) a notice of the prosecutor’s right to vary or terminate the agreement with the approval of the court; and
-- src:14943 | (p) an indication of the deadline by which the organization must meet the terms of the agreement.
@ref s 715.34(1) (src:14924-14943)
DECLARE `s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` HAS
    `(a) a statement of facts related to the offence that the organization is alleged to have committed and an undertaking by the organization not to make or condone any public statement that contradicts those facts`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b) the organization’s admission of responsibility for the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c) an indication of the obligation for the organization to provide any other information that will assist in identifying any person involved in the act or omission, or any wrongdoing related to that act or omission, that the organization becomes aware of, or can obtain through reasonable efforts, after the agreement has been entered into`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(d) an indication of the obligation for the organization to cooperate in any investigation, prosecution or other proceeding in Canada, or elsewhere if the prosecutor considers it appropriate, resulting from the act or omission, including by providing information or testimony`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(e) the agreement identifies any property, benefit or advantage obtained or derived directly or indirectly from the act or omission`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(e)(i) an obligation for the organization to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of Canada, to be disposed of in accordance with paragraph 4(1)(b.2) of the Seized Property Management Act`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(e)(ii) an obligation for the organization to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of a province, to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(e)(iii) an obligation for the organization to otherwise deal with it, as the prosecutor directs`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(f) an indication of the obligation for the organization to pay a penalty to the Receiver General or to the treasurer of a province, as the case may be, for each offence to which the agreement applies, the amount to be paid and any other terms respecting payment`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(g) an indication of any reparations, including restitution consistent with paragraph 738(1)(a) or (b), that the organization is required to make to a victim`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(g) a statement by the prosecutor of the reasons why reparations to a victim are not appropriate in the circumstances`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(g) an indication of any measure required in lieu of reparations to a victim`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(h) an indication of the obligation for the organization to pay a victim surcharge for each offence to which the agreement applies, other than an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, the amount to be paid and any other terms respecting payment`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(h) every offence to which the agreement applies is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i) an indication of the obligation for the organization to report to the prosecutor on the implementation of the agreement`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i) an indication of the manner in which the report is to be made and any other terms respecting reporting`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(j) an indication of the legal effects of the agreement`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(k) an acknowledgement by the organization that the agreement has been made in good faith and that the information it has provided during the negotiation is accurate and complete`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(k) a commitment that the organization will continue to provide accurate and complete information while the agreement is in force`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(l) an indication of the use that can be made of information obtained as a result of the agreement, subject to subsection (2)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(m) a warning that the breach of any term of the agreement may lead to an application by the prosecutor for termination of the agreement and a recommencement of proceedings`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(n) an indication of the obligation for the organization not to deduct, for income tax purposes, the costs of any reparations or other measures referred to in paragraph (g) or any other costs incurred to fulfil the terms of the agreement`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(o) a notice of the prosecutor’s right to vary or terminate the agreement with the approval of the court`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(p) an indication of the deadline by which the organization must meet the terms of the agreement`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 715.34(1) (src:14924-14943)
GIVEN agreement IS A `s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` MEANS
    IF     agreement's `(a) a statement of facts related to the offence that the organization is alleged to have committed and an undertaking by the organization not to make or condone any public statement that contradicts those facts`
       AND agreement's `(b) the organization’s admission of responsibility for the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence`
       AND agreement's `(c) an indication of the obligation for the organization to provide any other information that will assist in identifying any person involved in the act or omission, or any wrongdoing related to that act or omission, that the organization becomes aware of, or can obtain through reasonable efforts, after the agreement has been entered into`
       AND agreement's `(d) an indication of the obligation for the organization to cooperate in any investigation, prosecution or other proceeding in Canada, or elsewhere if the prosecutor considers it appropriate, resulting from the act or omission, including by providing information or testimony`
       AND `paragraph (e) is met`
       AND agreement's `(f) an indication of the obligation for the organization to pay a penalty to the Receiver General or to the treasurer of a province, as the case may be, for each offence to which the agreement applies, the amount to be paid and any other terms respecting payment`
       AND `paragraph (g) is met`
       AND `paragraph (h) is met`
       AND agreement's `(i) an indication of the obligation for the organization to report to the prosecutor on the implementation of the agreement`
       AND agreement's `(i) an indication of the manner in which the report is to be made and any other terms respecting reporting`
       AND agreement's `(j) an indication of the legal effects of the agreement`
       AND agreement's `(k) an acknowledgement by the organization that the agreement has been made in good faith and that the information it has provided during the negotiation is accurate and complete`
       AND agreement's `(k) a commitment that the organization will continue to provide accurate and complete information while the agreement is in force`
       AND agreement's `(l) an indication of the use that can be made of information obtained as a result of the agreement, subject to subsection (2)`
       AND agreement's `(m) a warning that the breach of any term of the agreement may lead to an application by the prosecutor for termination of the agreement and a recommencement of proceedings`
       AND agreement's `(n) an indication of the obligation for the organization not to deduct, for income tax purposes, the costs of any reparations or other measures referred to in paragraph (g) or any other costs incurred to fulfil the terms of the agreement`
       AND agreement's `(o) a notice of the prosecutor’s right to vary or terminate the agreement with the approval of the court`
       AND agreement's `(p) an indication of the deadline by which the organization must meet the terms of the agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A remediation agreement must include"
    WHERE
        -- (e): with respect to any property, benefit or advantage identified in the agreement ... an obligation to (i) forfeit it to Canada, (ii) forfeit it to a province, or (iii) otherwise deal with it. Where none is identified there is nothing to deal with.
        `paragraph (e) is met` MEANS
            IF agreement's `(e) the agreement identifies any property, benefit or advantage obtained or derived directly or indirectly from the act or omission`
            THEN agreement's `(e)(i) an obligation for the organization to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of Canada, to be disposed of in accordance with paragraph 4(1)(b.2) of the Seized Property Management Act`
                 OR agreement's `(e)(ii) an obligation for the organization to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of a province, to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs`
                 OR agreement's `(e)(iii) an obligation for the organization to otherwise deal with it, as the prosecutor directs`
            ELSE TRUE
        -- (g): an indication of any reparations ... OR a statement of the reasons why reparations are not appropriate AND an indication of any measure required in lieu (fork F5: how "and" binds).
        `paragraph (g) is met` MEANS
                agreement's `(g) an indication of any reparations, including restitution consistent with paragraph 738(1)(a) or (b), that the organization is required to make to a victim`
            OR (    agreement's `(g) a statement by the prosecutor of the reasons why reparations to a victim are not appropriate in the circumstances`
                AND agreement's `(g) an indication of any measure required in lieu of reparations to a victim`)
        -- (h): a victim surcharge for each offence to which the agreement applies, other than an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act.
        `paragraph (h) is met` MEANS
                agreement's `(h) every offence to which the agreement applies is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`
            OR agreement's `(h) an indication of the obligation for the organization to pay a victim surcharge for each offence to which the agreement applies, other than an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, the amount to be paid and any other terms respecting payment`

-- 715.34 (2) No admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission made by the organization as a result of the agreement is admissible in evidence against that organization
-- in any civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission, except those contained in the statement of facts and admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b), if the agreement is approved by the court.
-- src:14945 | (2) No admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission made by the organization as a result of the agreement is admissible in evidence against that organization in any civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission, except those contained in the statement of facts and admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b), if the agreement is approved by the court.
@ref s 715.34(2) (src:14945-14945)
GIVEN `it is an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made by the organization as a result of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is offered in evidence against that organization in civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is contained in the statement of facts and admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is approved by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.34(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission` AND `it was made by the organization as a result of the agreement` AND `it is offered in evidence against that organization in civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "made by the organization as a result of the agreement is admissible in evidence against that organization in any civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission"
        IF `it is contained in the statement of facts and admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b)` AND `the agreement is approved by the court` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except those contained in the statement of facts and admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b), if the agreement is approved by the court"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 715.34 (3) A remediation agreement may include, among other things, (a) compliance measures; (b) reimbursement of the prosecutor's costs; (c) an independent monitor. "Among other things": the list is not closed.
-- src:14947 | (3) A remediation agreement may include, among other things,
-- src:14948 | (a) an indication of the obligation for the organization to establish, implement or enhance compliance measures to address any deficiencies in the organization’s policies, standards or procedures — including those related to internal control procedures and employee training — that may have allowed the act or omission;
-- src:14949 | (b) an indication of the obligation for the organization to reimburse the prosecutor for any costs identified in the agreement that are related to its administration and that have or will be incurred by the prosecutor; and
-- src:14950 | (c) an indication of the fact that an independent monitor has been appointed, as selected with the prosecutor’s approval, to verify and report to the prosecutor on the organization’s compliance with the obligation referred to in paragraph (a), or any other obligation in the agreement identified by the prosecutor, as well as an indication of the organization’s obligations with respect to that monitor, including the obligations to cooperate with the monitor and pay the monitor’s costs.
@ref s 715.34(3) (src:14947-14950)
DECLARE `s 715.34(3) the term` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.34(3)(a) an indication of the obligation for the organization to establish, implement or enhance compliance measures to address any deficiencies in the organization’s policies, standards or procedures — including those related to internal control procedures and employee training — that may have allowed the act or omission`
    `s 715.34(3)(b) an indication of the obligation for the organization to reimburse the prosecutor for any costs identified in the agreement that are related to its administration and that have or will be incurred by the prosecutor`
    `s 715.34(3)(c) an indication of the fact that an independent monitor has been appointed, as selected with the prosecutor’s approval, to verify and report to the prosecutor on the organization’s compliance`
    `s 715.34(3) a term that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names`

@ref s 715.34(3) (src:14947-14950)
GIVEN term IS A `s 715.34(3) the term`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.34(3) the remediation agreement may include the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `s 715.34(3)(a) an indication of the obligation for the organization to establish, implement or enhance compliance measures to address any deficiencies in the organization’s policies, standards or procedures — including those related to internal control procedures and employee training — that may have allowed the act or omission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.34(3)(b) an indication of the obligation for the organization to reimburse the prosecutor for any costs identified in the agreement that are related to its administration and that have or will be incurred by the prosecutor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.34(3)(c) an indication of the fact that an independent monitor has been appointed, as selected with the prosecutor’s approval, to verify and report to the prosecutor on the organization’s compliance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.34(3) a term that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may include, among other things"

§ `Section 715.35 -- Independent monitor: conflict of interest`

-- 715.35 A candidate for appointment as an independent monitor must notify the prosecutor in writing of any previous or ongoing relationship, in particular with the organization or any of its representatives,
-- that may have a real or perceived impact on the candidate's ability to provide an independent verification. The core's Party type has no candidate-monitor constructor (NEEDS-CORE.md): this rule uses a type of its own.
-- src:14952 | 715.35 A candidate for appointment as an independent monitor must notify the prosecutor in writing of any previous or ongoing relationship, in particular with the organization or any of its representatives, that may have a real or perceived impact on the candidate’s ability to provide an independent verification.
@ref s 715.35 (src:14952-14952)
GIVEN `the person is a candidate for appointment as an independent monitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate has a previous or ongoing relationship, in particular with the organization or any of its representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship may have a real or perceived impact on the candidate’s ability to provide an independent verification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.35 the candidate must notify the prosecutor in writing of the relationship` MEANS
    IF `the person is a candidate for appointment as an independent monitor` AND `the candidate has a previous or ongoing relationship, in particular with the organization or any of its representatives` AND `the relationship may have a real or perceived impact on the candidate’s ability to provide an independent verification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any previous or ongoing relationship, in particular with the organization or any of its representatives, that may have a real or perceived impact on the candidate’s ability to provide an independent verification"

§ `Regulative rules of sections 715.32 to 715.35 (the same duties and permissions, run with #TRACE in the tests file)`

-- Each rule below is the duty, permission or bar ONCE IT HAS ARISEN, and carries no gate. The conditions under which it arises ("if", "where", "when", "after") are tested by the decision function of the same section, and the #TRACE runs in the tests file show what follows from doing or not doing the act, never whether the duty arose.

-- Parties are the core's Party type, except the candidate monitor (a type of its own). No deadline, consequence or remedy is added that the text does not state:
-- where the text gives no time limit the rule has no WITHIN, so a duty not yet performed shows as a standing obligation and never as a breach.
DECLARE `s 715.35 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.35 a candidate for appointment as an independent monitor`

DECLARE `s 715.32 to 715.35 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.32(1) enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement`
    `s 715.32(2) consider the factors`
    `s 715.32(3) consider the national economic interest, the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada or the identity of the organization or individual involved`
    `s 715.33(1) give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations`
    `s 715.35 notify the prosecutor in writing of the relationship`

-- src:14891 | 715.32 (1) The prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement with an organization alleged to have committed an offence if the following conditions are met:
@ref s 715.32(1) (src:14891-14891)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 715.32 to 715.35 act`
`s 715.32(1) the prosecutor's permission to enter into negotiations` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MAY `s 715.32(1) enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement`

-- src:14897 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), the prosecutor must consider the following factors:
@ref s 715.32(2) (src:14897-14897)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 715.32 to 715.35 act`
`s 715.32(2) the prosecutor's duty to consider the factors` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 715.32(2) consider the factors`

-- src:14908 | (3) Despite paragraph (2)(i), if the organization is alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, the prosecutor must not consider the national economic interest, the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada or the identity of the organization or individual involved.
@ref s 715.32(3) (src:14908-14908)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 715.32 to 715.35 act`
`s 715.32(3) the prosecutor's prohibition on considering the national economic interest` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    SHANT `s 715.32(3) consider the national economic interest, the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada or the identity of the organization or individual involved`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the prosecutor` BECAUSE "s 715.32(3): the prosecutor considered a matter that the subsection bars"

-- src:14910 | 715.33 (1) If the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement, they must give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations and the notice must include
@ref s 715.33(1) (src:14910-14910)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 715.32 to 715.35 act`
`s 715.33(1) the prosecutor's duty to give written notice` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 715.33(1) give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations`

-- src:14952 | 715.35 A candidate for appointment as an independent monitor must notify the prosecutor in writing of any previous or ongoing relationship, in particular with the organization or any of its representatives, that may have a real or perceived impact on the candidate’s ability to provide an independent verification.
@ref s 715.35 (src:14952-14952)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 715.35 party` `s 715.32 to 715.35 act`
`s 715.35 the candidate's duty to notify the prosecutor` MEANS
    PARTY `s 715.35 a candidate for appointment as an independent monitor`
    MUST `s 715.35 notify the prosecutor in writing of the relationship`
